## When the watcher fires

**5. Bash, foreground:**
```
herdr agent get rdp-audio
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 120
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio status --short
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio log --oneline origin/main..HEAD
```
If it stopped before task 9 (blocked, or a question), I resolve that first. If context is under 20%, I first send `herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "/compact keep: plan path, branch, task 7-9 results, test commands" --wait --until idle`.

**6. Bash, foreground:**
```
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "<brief>" --wait --until working --timeout 60000
```
Brief:
> New operator task, same worktree and branch (feat/rdp-audio). Tasks 7–9 stay as committed; do not amend them.
> Task 10: fix the noVNC keyboard-layout bug in roles/desktop. Symptom as recorded: <pasted verbatim from step 2>.
> Mandatory skills, named in your report: superpowers:systematic-debugging (root cause with evidence before any change), superpowers:test-driven-development (failing offline test under projects/ccs/tests/ first), superpowers:verification-before-completion.
> Constraints: separate commit(s) `fix(desktop): …`; no host or VM access; only `--syntax-check` runs; bash only; idempotent; no session links. Editing the xstartup template triggers `Restart tigervnc` on deploy, so state explicitly whether you touched it. If the root cause cannot be established offline, stop and report what live evidence you need. Do not guess.
> Report: root cause, files changed, RED and GREEN output, commit SHAs. Reply in English.

**7. Bash, background:** `herdr agent wait rdp-audio --timeout 5400000`. Then I update the backlog to "in progress".

## Why

Text typed into a working Claude Code session is injected at its next tool call. Prompting now would steer it mid-task 7, between RED and GREEN, which is exactly the interruption you ruled out. So delivery waits for a clean boundary.

The watcher runs in the background because a foreground wait blocks my session, caps at 10 minutes, and makes me unreachable to you.

You already decided who does the work and on which branch, so there is no advisor vote and no poll. I only report the consequences.

I check the commits before sending because "idle" does not prove tasks 7–9 are finished. I compact at the boundary because 30% context will not survive three tasks plus a debugging session, and an auto-compact mid-debug loses evidence.
